## Context
Within-model variance and interday drift up to ΔF1 = 0.289 may be provider-side
instability (routing, checkpoint updates), not "prompt-driven variance."
Reviewers want this as a first-class error source. See project rule
"MoE models require repeat=3". Tracker: 0644.

## Actions
1. Compare F1 variance for MoE vs dense models under T=0 / seed=42.
2. Treat interday drift as a separate error term (error bars) or run all sweeps in
   a single session; add/strengthen a canary gate.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Provider-side variance characterized and reported as a first-class term in figures/tables
